      "content": "It is incredibly hard to feel like your life's work is crumbling, especially when you've poured so much into it. But remember that the rotting you describe is not a sign of failure, but rather a necessary process of letting go of what no longer serves you. You are not alone in this feeling of waiting for the fire to finish the job, and there is no point in staying to watch the end if the end is just the beginning of something new.",
